    "4191532093": {
      "id": 4191532093,
      "path": ".github/workflows/Generate-StyleGuideArtifacts.ps1",
      "line": 1718,
      "body": "The new `unknown-artifact` failure is terse and loses the actionable context previously provided by `ValidateSet` binding errors. Consider throwing a more diagnostic message that includes the invalid `ArtifactId` and the allowed IDs (e.g., derived from `$DestinationMap.Keys`) so callers can quickly self-correct without debugging.",
      "commit_id": "7dd48f52c9e4c17268b4a571919622f4d701e5d0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/franklesniak/TerraformStyleGuide/pull/68#discussion_r4191532093"
    },
    "4191532114": {
      "id": 4191532114,
      "path": ".github/workflows/Generate-StyleGuideArtifacts.ps1",
      "line": 1734,
      "body": "The new `unknown-artifact` failure is terse and loses the actionable context previously provided by `ValidateSet` binding errors. Consider throwing a more diagnostic message that includes the invalid `ArtifactId` and the allowed IDs (e.g., derived from `$DestinationMap.Keys`) so callers can quickly self-correct without debugging.",
      "commit_id": "7dd48f52c9e4c17268b4a571919622f4d701e5d0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/franklesniak/TerraformStyleGuide/pull/68#discussion_r4191532114"
    },
    "4191532133": {
      "id": 4191532133,
      "path": ".github/workflows/Test-StyleGuideArtifacts.ps1",
      "line": 593,
      "body": "The Node executable path is no longer validated after `Get-Command`. If `Source` resolves to a non-existent path (or an unexpected shim), the later `Process.Start()` failure will be harder to diagnose and may produce a different error surface than intended. Add an explicit `[IO.File]::Exists($strSemanticNodePath)` check and throw the existing fixed diagnostic when missing (similar to the prior implementation).",
      "commit_id": "7dd48f52c9e4c17268b4a571919622f4d701e5d0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/franklesniak/TerraformStyleGuide/pull/68#discussion_r4191532133"
    },
    "4191532148": {
      "id": 4191532148,
      "path": ".github/workflows/Test-StyleGuideArtifacts.ps1",
      "line": 190,
      "body": "`ConvertFrom-NulPathRecordStream` now emits one `byte[]` per record (or no output for empty input), but the `OutputType` attribute was broadened to `[System.Array]` while the function documentation still states `System.Byte[]`. To keep contract documentation precise, update `OutputType` (and/or the docstring) to reflect that it outputs `System.Byte[]` objects.",
      "commit_id": "7dd48f52c9e4c17268b4a571919622f4d701e5d0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/franklesniak/TerraformStyleGuide/pull/68#discussion_r4191532148"
    },
    "4191532171": {
      "id": 4191532171,
      "path": ".github/workflows/build.yml",
      "line": 11,
      "body": "The Windows 5.1 and Windows 7 generator jobs appear to duplicate substantial inline acquisition + proof logic (differing mainly by shell/ExpectedHost). This duplication increases the risk of the two drifting over time. If policy constraints allow, consider factoring the shared logic into a reusable unit (YAML anchor/alias, a composite action, or a checked-in helper script invoked by both jobs) so future fixes are applied once.",
      "commit_id": "7dd48f52c9e4c17268b4a571919622f4d701e5d0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/franklesniak/TerraformStyleGuide/pull/68#discussion_r4191532171"
    },
    "4191532191": {
      "id": 4191532191,
      "path": ".github/workflows/build.yml",
      "line": 139,
      "body": "The Windows 5.1 and Windows 7 generator jobs appear to duplicate substantial inline acquisition + proof logic (differing mainly by shell/ExpectedHost). This duplication increases the risk of the two drifting over time. If policy constraints allow, consider factoring the shared logic into a reusable unit (YAML anchor/alias, a composite action, or a checked-in helper script invoked by both jobs) so future fixes are applied once.",
      "commit_id": "7dd48f52c9e4c17268b4a571919622f4d701e5d0",
